/**

@page benchmarks_exahype2_advection_kernel_benchmarks Benchmarks of Compute Kernels for the Advection Equation

We provide example plots of outputs obtained from Leonardo.

The benchmarks
were run with a 2D advection setup using 2048 patches per kernel launch,
32 compute threads, 1 launching thread and 16 finite volumes per axis.
The maximal eigenvalue has been evaluated and we took 100 measurements samples.

The following Python command was used:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    python3 kernel-benchmarks-fv-rusanov.py --dim 2 --patch-size 16 --num-patches 2048 -e
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

We show the best case throughputs.

## Host
@image html plot_advection_Leonardo_host.png

## Device (using OpenMP GPU offloading)
@image html plot_advection_Leonardo_device_omp.png

*/
